# Architecture Design

## System Architecture Overview

The Sales Intelligence Platform follows a layered, modular architecture with clear separation of concerns.

## Layer Architecture

### Presentation Layer (Frontend - Next.js)

- Natural language search interface
- Excel-like data grid components
- File upload handlers
- Real-time agent activity display
- Authentication UI (login/signup)

### Application Layer (Backend - Node.js)

- RESTful API endpoints
- JWT authentication middleware
- Request validation and sanitization
- Rate limiting and security
- Error handling and logging

### Business Logic Layer

- Multi-agent orchestration (LangGraph)
- Scraping engine (3-agent system)
- Data processing and validation
- Online search integration
- File processors (Excel, HAR)

### Data Layer

- PostgreSQL database
- ORM/Query builder
- Migration management
- Connection pooling
- Transaction management

### Integration Layer

- Gemini API client
- Web search API integration
- LinkedIn data scraping
- External API connectors

## Multi-Agent System Architecture

### Conversational Agent Layer

#### Intent Recognition Agent

- Analyzes user input
- Determines query type (1-5)
- Extracts key entities and parameters

#### Context Management Agent

- Maintains conversation history
- Tracks user session state
- Provides context to other agents

#### Router Agent

- Routes requests to appropriate execution pipeline
- Manages agent workflow orchestration
- Handles parallel and sequential execution

#### Database Query Agent

- Executes database searches
- Formats results for display
- Handles complex queries with joins

#### Scraper Controller Agent

- Manages scraping workflow
- Triggers Analysis, Implementation, Validation agents
- Monitors scraping progress

#### File Processor Agent

- Detects file type (Excel vs HAR)
- Routes to appropriate parser
- Handles column mapping for Excel
- Parses HAR files for scraping data

#### Online Search Agent

- Searches web when data not in database
- Finds LinkedIn profiles
- Extracts and validates information
- Adds verified data to database

#### Response Formatter Agent

- Formats data for Excel-like display
- Generates natural language responses
- Handles error messages
- Provides progress updates

### Scraping Agent Layer

#### Analysis Agent

- Analyzes target website structure
- Detects content type (static, SPA, API-based)
- Determines optimal scraping strategy
- Checks for authentication requirements

#### Implementation Agent

- Executes chosen scraping strategy
- Methods: CSS selectors, HAR processing, OCR/ML, API calls
- Handles pagination and dynamic content
- Extracts structured data

#### Validation Agent

- Validates scraped data accuracy
- Verifies expected data count
- Checks logical consistency
- Triggers retry with different method if validation fails
- Updates database only after validation success

## Database Architecture

### Core Tables

#### people

- id (UUID, Primary Key)
- first_name
- last_name
- email (unique, indexed)
- phone
- linkedin_url (unique, indexed)
- title
- company_id (Foreign Key to companies)
- location
- data_source
- created_at
- updated_at

#### companies

- id (UUID, Primary Key)
- name (indexed)
- domain (unique, indexed)
- industry
- size
- location
- linkedin_url (unique, indexed)
- description
- data_source
- created_at
- updated_at

#### scraping_jobs

- id (UUID, Primary Key)
- url
- status (pending, in_progress, completed, failed)
- strategy_used
- records_extracted
- validation_status
- error_message
- created_at
- completed_at

#### user_sessions

- id (UUID, Primary Key)
- user_id (Foreign Key to users)
- conversation_history (JSONB)
- active
- created_at
- updated_at

#### users

- id (UUID, Primary Key)
- email (unique, indexed)
- password_hash
- role
- created_at
- last_login

### Relationships

- people.company_id → companies.id
- scraping_jobs → generates records in people/companies
- user_sessions.user_id → users.id

## API Architecture

### Authentication Endpoints

- POST /api/auth/register
- POST /api/auth/login
- POST /api/auth/refresh
- POST /api/auth/logout

### Query Endpoints

- POST /api/query (main conversational endpoint)
- POST /api/query/file (file upload endpoint)
- GET /api/query/status/:jobId

### Data Endpoints

- GET /api/people (with filters, pagination)
- GET /api/people/:id
- GET /api/companies (with filters, pagination)
- GET /api/companies/:id

### Scraping Endpoints

- POST /api/scrape/url
- POST /api/scrape/har
- GET /api/scrape/jobs/:id

### Export Endpoints

- POST /api/export/excel
- POST /api/export/csv

## Security Architecture

### Authentication

- JWT access tokens (15 min expiry)
- Refresh tokens (7 day expiry)
- Secure HTTP-only cookies
- Token rotation on refresh

### Authorization

- Role-based access control
- Resource-level permissions
- API key management

### Input Validation

- Schema validation on all endpoints
- SQL injection prevention
- XSS protection
- File upload validation

### Data Security

- Encrypted passwords (bcrypt)
- Environment variable secrets
- HTTPS enforcement
- CORS configuration

## Performance Architecture

### Caching Strategy

- In-memory caching for frequent queries
- Database query result caching
- API response caching

### Async Processing

- Background job queue for scraping
- Parallel agent execution
- Non-blocking I/O operations

### Database Optimization

- Proper indexing strategy
- Connection pooling
- Query optimization
- Read replicas for scaling
